// src/std/actor/actor.zen
//
// The actor surface: the types a behavior's signature is written in.
// Actors are the only concurrency primitive — no async/await, no
// locks, no user-facing threads — and DESIGN.md's three guarantees
// are what replace every lock:
//
//   one message at a time per actor -> actor state is single-threaded
//   causal ordering                 -> A's messages to B arrive in order
//   only val / iso cross actors     -> data races are compile errors
//
// WHAT IS HERE IS THE SURFACE, AND THE FLOOR IS OWED. No runtime is
// written: `Env.spawn` has no lowering, a behavior call on a `Ref`
// enqueues nothing, there is no mailbox and no scheduler. Read this
// file the way `Net` and `Threads` in env.zen are read — a declared
// capability whose floor a later stage writes.
//
// IT IS NOT ORNAMENTAL FOR ALL THAT. `env.zen` declares
// `spawn* = <A: Actor>(self: @Self, actor: A) Ref<A>`, and once a
// bodiless signature resolves its own names (#810) a standard library
// naming two types nothing declares stops compiling: `zen build src`
// reported `undefined name Actor` and `undefined name Ref` at
// env.zen:216. These declarations are what make that signature true.
//
// The runtime's own tests stay deferred and are the honest scoreboard:
// tests/corpus/own/val_literal_crosses_actor, own/send_consumed_buffer,
// must-fail/own/send_ref, must-fail/own/use_after_send and example/src
// all carry `.stage 5`. The day one of them passes is the day the
// runtime is real; nothing in this file moves any of them.

Env = std.env
Alloc = std.mem

// A send that had nowhere to land, and there is no third way: the
// mailbox is bounded, so either a sender outran its receiver (`Full`)
// or the actor stopped while an address to it was still held
// (`Closed`). Neither names a cause — a sender learns that the
// message did not arrive, which is the whole of what it can act on.
ActorError* = Closed | Full

// The ADDRESS of an actor, never the actor. Freely sendable, and a
// behavior call on one IS a send: `foo.say("hi")` enqueues and
// returns immediately, so a `Ref` is the only thing that crosses.
//
// `id` IS UNEXPORTED for `ArenaState`'s reason — what an address is
// made of is not part of what an address is. A program holds a Ref,
// hands it to another actor, and calls behaviors on it; nothing above
// this file has a use for the number underneath.
Ref*<A> = {
    id: u64,

    // Delivered AFTER the mailbox drains, so every message already
    // sent still runs and `stopped` is the last turn.
    //
    // `:` and not `::`, by the shallowness rule: the mailbox lives
    // behind the address, not in the handle's own two words — the
    // same reason `Alloc.raw` is `:` while allocating changes the
    // arena (DESIGN.md, "a handle's methods are `:`").
    stop* = (self: @Self) ()
}

// What a behavior is handed besides its own arguments: the authority
// it runs under. Neither half is ambient and neither is `main`'s — an
// actor draining its mailbox after `main` has returned still has both.
Context* = {
    // Authority flows from Env (law 2). STARRED because a behavior is
    // USER code living outside std, and `ctx.env.out.println(..)` is
    // how DESIGN.md's own actor example prints — an unstarred field
    // here would make the design's example unwritable.
    env*: Env,

    // The per-actor arena — pony's per-actor heap minus the GC —
    // rooted in the RUNTIME rather than in main's arena, and dropped
    // when the actor stops, freeing everything the actor made.
    // Starred for the reason `env` is: a behavior that allocates says
    // so in the code that allocates.
    alloc*: Alloc,
}

// The trait that makes a type spawnable, and the bound `Env.spawn`
// names. BOTH MEMBERS ARE OPTIONAL (`::=` with no body, as
// `Display.dump` is): an actor with no lifecycle work writes
// `Foo.impl(Actor, {})` and its behaviors are the other methods in
// that impl.
//
// THE BEHAVIORS ARE NOT LISTED HERE AND CANNOT BE. They are whatever
// methods the impl declares, and the message enum behind them is
// derived from their signatures at comptime — that derivation is
// `@meta` (docs/design_meta.md), which is why this file can be a
// surface today and a runtime only later.
Actor* = {
    // Runs on spawn, before the first message.
    started* ::= (self :: @Self, ctx: Context) ()

    // Runs after `stop()` has drained the mailbox — the last turn the
    // actor takes.
    stopped* ::= (self :: @Self, ctx: Context) ()
}
